    "explanation": "Transfer of learning occurs when knowledge or skill acquired in one setting improves performance in another. Near transfer involves similar tasks; far transfer requires recognizing a deeper principle across situations that may look quite different.\n\nTransfer is not automatic. It becomes more likely when learners compare cases, explain why a method works, encounter varied conditions, and practise choosing rather than merely repeating a procedure.",
