    "explanation": "Functional literacy is the capacity to understand and use written, numerical, and visual information in order to participate effectively in everyday, civic, educational, or work situations. It goes beyond decoding words to include locating, integrating, evaluating, and applying information.\n\nIts demands depend on context. A person may read fluent prose yet struggle with a timetable, form, contract, chart, or digital instruction. Literacy therefore includes knowing what a document is for and how its parts change a real decision.",
