    "explanation": "Metacognitive regulation is the active management of one's own learning through planning, monitoring, evaluation, and adjustment. It turns confusion, confidence, errors, and strategy use into information that can guide the next action.\n\nIt is most useful when it remains tied to a task. The aim is not constant introspection but better decisions about what to try, what to check, when to persist, and when to change course.",
    "explanationZh": "元认知调节是通过计划、监控、评价和调整，主动管理自身学习的能力。它把困惑、信心、错误和策略使用情况变成能够指导下一步行动的信息。\n\n它只有与具体任务相连时才真正有用。目标不是持续沉浸在自我分析里，而是更好地决定尝试什么、核查什么、何时坚持，以及何时改变方向。"
