    "explanation": "Deliberate practice is structured activity aimed at improving a clearly identified component of performance. It typically uses specific goals, tasks beyond comfortable automaticity, timely feedback, error correction, and sustained attention.\n\nIt differs from repetition, work experience, or performing familiar material. Those activities may maintain skill and still matter, but improvement requires practice that changes in response to evidence about the learner's current weakness.",
    "explanationZh": "刻意练习是以改善某个明确表现成分为目的的结构化活动。它通常包含具体目标、略高于舒适自动化水平的任务、及时反馈、错误修正和持续集中注意。\n\n它不同于单纯重复、积累工作年限或反复表演熟悉内容。这些活动可以维持技能，也有自身价值；真正的提升则要求练习根据当前弱点的证据不断改变。"
