    "explanation": "Emergent curriculum develops through an ongoing cycle of observing children's interests and theories, interpreting their learning, connecting it with educational goals, and deliberately planning environments, materials, questions, and documentation that extend inquiry.\n\nIt is not improvised teaching without objectives. Professional judgment is central: educators decide which interests contain sustained learning potential, how to include different children, what knowledge to introduce, and when an inquiry has reached a useful stopping point.",
    "explanationZh": "生成课程通过持续循环发展：观察儿童的兴趣与解释，判断其中的学习，把它与教育目标连接，再有意识地规划环境、材料、问题和记录方式，使探究继续深入。\n\n它不是没有目标的临场教学。教师的专业判断居于核心位置：哪些兴趣具有持续学习潜力，怎样让不同儿童进入活动，何时引入新知识，以及何时让探究在合适位置结束。"
