    "explanation": "Pedagogical content knowledge is the specialised knowledge teachers use to transform particular subject matter for learning. It includes representations, examples, analogies, explanations, task sequences, assessment approaches, and understanding of what learners commonly find difficult or misconceive.\n\nIt is distinct from subject knowledge alone and from general teaching technique alone. It lies in their interaction around a specific idea, learner group, and instructional context.",
