    "explanation": "Entrainment occurs when oscillating or rhythmic systems influence one another, or respond to an external periodic signal, so that their timing develops a stable relationship. Adjustment may involve phase, frequency, or both.\n\nEntrainment does not require identical motion or conscious imitation, and it operates only within conditions where coupling is strong enough relative to differences and disturbance. Musical pulse, movement, speech, and biological rhythms can display different forms of it.",
