    "explanation": "A deductive argument is valid when it is impossible for all its premises to be true while its conclusion is false. Validity evaluates the inferential relation and does not by itself establish that any premise is true.\n\nA sound argument is valid and has true premises; its conclusion must therefore be true. An invalid argument can have a true conclusion by coincidence, while a valid argument can lead from false premises to a false or even true conclusion.",
    "explanationZh": "一个演绎论证若不可能出现所有前提为真而结论为假的情形，就是有效的。有效性评价推断关系，本身并不证明任何前提为真。\n\n可靠论证既有效，又具有真实前提，因此结论必然为真。无效论证可能偶然得到真结论，有效论证也可能从假前提推出假结论，甚至推出碰巧为真的结论。"
