    "explanation": "Interlanguage is the developing linguistic system constructed by a language learner. It draws on prior languages and target-language input while also exhibiting internally generated rules, developmental sequences, communication strategies, and variability.\n\nLearner errors can therefore be systematic evidence rather than random failure. Interlanguage may reorganise, vary by task and attention, or fossilise when forms stabilise before becoming target-like.",
    "explanationZh": "中介语是语言学习者建构的、处于发展中的语言系统。它吸收既有语言与目标语输入，也呈现内部生成规则、发展顺序、交流策略和变异。\n\n因此，学习者错误可能是系统证据，而非随机失败。中介语会重组、随任务与注意变化，也可能在接近目标语以前因形式稳定而发生僵化。"
