    "explanation": "Arbitrariness of the sign means that no necessary natural bond connects most linguistic signifiers with the concepts they signify. Languages can therefore use different sound patterns and organise distinctions differently for comparable parts of experience.\n\nArbitrary does not mean individually optional or structurally random. Social convention, contrast with other signs, history, and repeated use stabilise meanings, while iconicity and sound symbolism show that some signs are partially motivated.",
    "explanationZh": "符号任意性指多数语言能指与其所指概念之间不存在必然自然联系。因此，不同语言可以用不同声音形式，也可以用不同方式组织相近经验中的区分。\n\n任意不等于个人可以随意选择，也不等于系统毫无结构。社会约定、与其他符号的对比、历史和反复使用会稳定意义；象似性与语音象征也说明部分符号具有一定动因。"
