    "explanation": "Pragmatics studies how utterance meaning depends on context, speaker intentions, shared assumptions, social relations, and inference beyond literal semantic content. It includes speech acts, implicature, presupposition, deixis, information structure, and politeness.\n\nContextual interpretation is constrained rather than arbitrary. Listeners use linguistic form and publicly available cues to infer what a speaker is doing, while clarification remains important when cues conflict or consequences are serious.",
