    "explanation": "Separation of powers distributes legislative, executive, judicial, or comparable governing functions among distinct institutions. Checks and balances give institutions ways to constrain, review, or depend on one another so authority cannot be concentrated without resistance.\n\nEffective separation requires practical independence, information, resources, and accountable procedures. Complete isolation is neither typical nor desirable, while poor design can produce deadlock, delay, or coordinated capture across formally separate bodies.",
