    "explanation": "Archival silence is a significant absence, marginalisation, or difficulty of retrieval within records and archives. Silences can arise when events are recorded, records selected, preserved or destroyed, collections described and opened, and histories later narrated.\n\nSilence is shaped by power but is not always deliberate, and an absent record does not prove an absent event. Ethical interpretation seeks alternative traces, tests their limits, respects affected communities, and avoids replacing omission with invented certainty.",
    "explanationZh": "档案沉默是记录与档案中具有意义的缺席、边缘化或检索困难。沉默可能在事件被记录、材料被选择、保存或毁损、馆藏被描述开放，以及历史被后来叙述时形成。\n\n沉默受权力塑造，却不总是故意；记录缺席也不证明事件缺席。合乎伦理的解释会寻找替代痕迹、检验其限制、尊重相关共同体，并避免用虚构确定性替换遗漏。"
