    "explanation": "The principal-agent problem arises when a principal delegates decisions or work to an agent whose interests are not perfectly aligned and whose information or actions are costly or impossible to observe fully.\n\nContracts, incentives, monitoring, governance, reputation, trust, and risk sharing can reduce agency costs, but narrow metrics invite distortion and strong incentives may transfer uncontrollable risk. Complete alignment is rarely costless or possible.",
    "explanationZh": "委托代理问题发生于委托人把决定或工作交给代理人，双方利益并不完全一致，而代理人的信息或行动又难以或无法被完整观察。\n\n合同、激励、监督、治理、声誉、信任与风险分担可以降低代理成本，但狭窄指标会诱发扭曲，过强激励也可能转移不可控风险。完全一致很少能够无成本实现。"
