    "explanation": "A community of practice is a group that shares a domain and develops knowledge through sustained participation in common activities, relationships, tools, stories, language, and problem solving. Learning includes movement toward fuller participation and identity.\n\nIt is more than a team, database, or informal gathering. Communities can preserve tacit judgement and innovate, but may also exclude newcomers or reproduce error, so access, challenge, documentation, and external connections matter.",
