    "explanation": "Gene-environment interaction occurs when the phenotypic effect associated with genetic differences depends on the environment, or when an environmental effect differs across genotypes. Non-parallel reaction norms are a common representation.\n\nIt is more specific than saying genes and environments both contribute. Conclusions depend on the genotypes, environments, traits, populations, and measurement scale studied; a statistical interaction is not by itself a molecular mechanism. Controlled designs are needed to separate interaction from correlated differences and confounding.",
