    "explanation": "Enzyme catalysis accelerates biochemical reactions by providing pathways with lower activation barriers. Binding, orientation, transition-state stabilisation, acid-base chemistry, and temporary covalent intermediates are among the mechanisms enzymes may use.\n\nEnzymes are regenerated overall and alter reaction rates rather than equilibrium or net Gibbs energy. Their activity can be specific and saturable and is shaped by substrate concentration, temperature, pH, cofactors, inhibitors, and regulation.",
    "explanationZh": "酶催化通过提供活化能垒更低的路径来加速生化反应。结合、定向、稳定过渡态、酸碱作用与暂时共价中间体，都是酶可能采用的机制。\n\n酶在总体反应后再生，改变的是反应速率，而非平衡位置或吉布斯自由能净变化。其活性可具有特异性和饱和性，并受底物浓度、温度、酸碱度、辅因子、抑制物与调控影响。"
