    "explanation": "Habitat fragmentation is the division of continuous habitat into smaller, more isolated patches, often together with habitat loss, edge effects, barriers, and changes in the surrounding matrix.\n\nEffects depend on total habitat amount, spatial configuration, scale, connectivity, matrix quality, and species ecology. Fragmentation per se must be evaluated separately from habitat amount. Avoiding intact-habitat loss is primary; corridors and crossings can improve movement but require targeted design, monitoring, and attention to transmitted risks.",
    "explanationZh": "栖息地破碎化是连续栖息地被分割成更小、更孤立的区块，并常与面积损失、边缘效应、屏障及周边基质变化同时发生。\n\n影响取决于栖息地总量、空间配置、尺度、连接度、基质质量与物种生态。必须把破碎化本身与栖息地总量分开评估。首要任务是避免完整栖息地损失；通道与过路设施可改善移动，却需定向设计、监测并关注同时传递的风险。"
