    "explanation": "Activation energy describes the energetic barrier to reaching a transition state along a reaction pathway. Thermodynamically favourable reactions can remain slow when few molecular encounters cross that barrier with suitable orientation.\n\nTemperature changes the distribution of molecular energies, and catalysts provide lower-barrier pathways. Neither action changes the overall free-energy difference between reactants and products, though temperature can also affect equilibrium.",
