    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Firework maker Ada used a fictional blue charge whose particle-count relation paired two red grain units with one silver crystal unit. Apprentice Bor added a second silver unit, believing more of the costly ingredient must make a deeper blue. The flare sputtered, and unused silver remained in the cup. Every finished charge required the same count relationship. Once the red grains were committed, extra silver had no partners with which to form additional product.\n\nThe particles were too small to count directly, and equal masses did not contain equal numbers because the building units had different masses. Ada converted weighed quantities into amounts of substance, then used the balanced reaction relation as a counting rule. Two units of red for every one of silver yielded one specified unit of charge in their model. The coefficients compared entities or moles; they did not say that two grams must combine with one gram.\n\nBor brought twelve red units and eight silver units. Red could support six product units, while silver could support eight, so red set the theoretical maximum and two silver units remained in excess. When he doubled only silver again, the maximum did not change. The expensive surplus therefore remained chemically idle and economically costly. When he added four red units instead, both ingredients could support eight charges. The limiting ingredient was identified by comparing each available amount with its required coefficient, not by choosing the smallest mass or volume.\n\nThe next batch produced only seven good charges although the calculation allowed eight. Some powder had spilled, one reagent was impure, and a side reaction formed smoke. Ada distinguished theoretical yield from actual yield and calculated percentage yield only after checking what had truly been measured. She also separated composition accounting from kinetics and equilibrium: a balanced relation constrained possible amounts but did not promise speed, completion, or a single pathway.\n\nBor eventually scaled the recipe to a hundred flares. He carried units through every conversion, included solution concentration and purity, and kept measurement uncertainty from pretending to be exact particles. A tiny rounding error repeated at each stage could leave an entire box unmatched. He planned modest process allowance without changing the underlying ratio and recorded excess material for recovery rather than hiding it as waste.\n\nAda was teaching stoichiometry: quantitative relations among reactants and products derived from a balanced chemical equation and conservation of atoms, charge, and relevant building units. Mole ratios connect measurable amounts to particle-level counts; the limiting reactant sets the theoretical yield, while excess remains. Actual yield can be lower because of incomplete reaction, side reactions, loss, or impurity. Bor's extra spoon had not created more blue. It had obscured which ingredient had already run out.",
    "storyBodyZh": "烟火师阿达用一种虚构蓝色药剂，其粒子计数关系是两单位红粒配一单位银晶。学徒博尔又加一单位银晶，以为昂贵原料越多，蓝色必然越深。焰火却只发出断续光，杯底还留着未用银晶。每份成品都要求相同数量关系，红粒全部投入后，多余银晶已找不到伙伴形成更多产物。\n\n粒子小得无法直接计数，等质量也不包含相等数量，因为组成单位质量不同。阿达先把称得的量转换成物质的量，再把配平反应关系当作计数规则。在他们的模型中，每两单位红粒配一单位银晶，得到一单位指定药剂。系数比较的是实体或摩尔，不是说两克必然与一克结合。\n\n博尔带来十二单位红粒和八单位银晶。红粒只够形成六单位产物，银晶能支持八单位，因此红粒决定理论上限，剩两单位银晶过量。只把银晶再翻倍，上限仍不改变，昂贵剩余物既没有化学贡献，也增加经济成本。若改为补四单位红粒，两种原料便都能支持八份。限制原料要把每项可用量与所需系数比较，不能按最小质量或体积判断。\n\n下一批计算可得八份，实际却只有七份合格药剂。部分粉末洒落，一种原料不纯，还有副反应生成烟雾。阿达区分理论产率与实际产率，并在核实真正测量内容后才计算百分产率。她也把组成核算与动力学、平衡分开：配平关系限制可能数量，却不承诺速度、完全反应或只有一条路径。\n\n博尔最终把配方扩大到一百枚焰火。他在每次换算中保留单位，计入溶液浓度与纯度，也不让测量不确定性伪装成精确粒子数。每一步重复的小舍入误差，最后可能留下整箱无法配对的原料。他设置适度工艺余量，却不改底层比例，并登记多余材料以便回收，而非把它藏成浪费。\n\n阿达教授的是化学计量：依据配平化学方程式与原子、电荷及相关组成单位守恒，确定反应物和产物之间的定量关系。摩尔比把可测量的量连接到粒子计数，限制反应物决定理论产率，过量部分则会剩余。实际产率还可能因反应不完全、副反应、损失或杂质而降低。博尔多加的一勺没有创造更多蓝光，只是遮住了哪种原料早已用完。",
    "explanation": "Stoichiometry uses balanced chemical equations and conservation to relate quantities of reactants and products. Equation coefficients express particle or mole ratios, which must be combined with molar mass, concentration, purity, and units when using measured material.\n\nThe limiting reactant determines theoretical yield; other reactants may remain in excess. Actual yield can be lower through incomplete conversion, competing reactions, impurity, and process loss, while a balanced equation alone says nothing about rate.",
    "explanationZh": "化学计量依据配平方程与守恒关系，把反应物和产物数量联系起来。方程系数表达粒子比或摩尔比，处理实测材料时还要结合摩尔质量、浓度、纯度与单位。\n\n限制反应物决定理论产率，其他反应物可能过量。反应不完全、竞争反应、杂质与过程损失会让实际产率更低，而配平方程本身并不说明反应速率。"
