    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Icehouse owner Elan opened the partition between a warm storeroom and a chamber of ice. Heat passed into the cold side until temperatures approached one another and some ice melted. Total energy had merely moved within the building. Elan therefore expected that, if he waited, the same energy would spontaneously gather back in the warm room and the melted water would refreeze. The building never performed that reverse history.\n\nPhysicist Nera scattered dark and pale beads across a divided tray to represent small parcels of energy. There were very few arrangements in which almost all dark beads occupied one side and pale beads the other, but enormously many mixed arrangements with similar macroscopic balance. Random microscopic motion could in principle fluctuate either way, yet an isolated collection with many particles overwhelmingly moved toward macrostates compatible with more microscopic arrangements. The reverse was not forbidden by the energy ledger; it was fantastically improbable at ordinary scale.\n\nElan bought a refrigerator and triumphantly moved heat from the cold chamber to the warmer outdoors. Nera pointed to the power cable and the hot condenser. The device used work and expelled more heat outside than it removed from within. The chamber's measure could decrease locally while the combined device and surroundings increased overall. Moving heat from cold to hot was possible, but not as a costless cyclic process whose only result reversed spontaneous heat flow.\n\nA second dispute involved two gases separated by a partition. Once mixed, they did not sort themselves back by colour, although a carefully operated membrane could separate them by consuming work and producing effects elsewhere. Friction likewise turned organised motion into dispersed molecular motion. Recovering every microscopic correlation would require impossible control. Macroscopic irreversibility emerged from statistics, lost correlations, and constraints even though underlying microscopic laws could often be reversible.\n\nNera refused to define the quantity merely as messiness. A shuffled deck could look disorderly without constituting a thermodynamic system, and crystals still possessed thermal states. In classical thermodynamics, reversible heat transfer divided by temperature helped define changes; in statistical mechanics, the logarithm of compatible microscopic states linked the same quantity to probability. Its increase law applied to isolated systems, while open systems could export it and build local structure by consuming free energy.\n\nThe icehouse displayed entropy: a thermodynamic state function connected to energy dispersal and, statistically, to the number of microscopic configurations compatible with a macrostate. For an isolated macroscopic system in the thermodynamic description, total entropy does not decrease; spontaneous processes tend toward overwhelmingly more probable macrostates, while tiny systems may fluctuate. Local decreases are possible when larger increases occur elsewhere, as in refrigeration or living systems. Energy conservation explained why nothing vanished. Entropy explained why the cold did not simply walk home and restore yesterday's arrangement.",
    "storyBodyZh": "冰窖主人埃兰打开温暖储藏室与冰室之间的隔板。热量流入冷侧，直到两边温度接近，部分冰也融化。总能量只是在建筑内部移动，埃兰因此期待，只要等待，同一批能量会自行聚回暖室，融水也会重新结冰。建筑始终没有演出这段反向历史。\n\n物理学者奈拉在分隔托盘上撒开深浅两色珠子，代表微小能量份额。几乎所有深珠集中一侧、浅珠集中另一侧的排列很少，宏观上均匀混合的微观排列却多得惊人。随机微观运动原则上可向任一方向波动，但含大量粒子的孤立集合压倒性地走向兼容更多微观排列的宏观状态。能量账本没有禁止反向，普通尺度下它只是罕见得近乎不会发生。\n\n埃兰买来制冷机，得意地把热从冷室搬到更暖的室外。奈拉指向电源线与发热冷凝器。机器消耗功，向外排出的热比从室内移走的更多。冷室的该项度量可以局部下降，设备与环境合计却总体上升。热可以从冷处搬向热处，却不能成为无代价循环，其唯一结果只是逆转自发热流。\n\n第二场争论涉及被隔板分开的两种气体。隔板移除后，它们不会自行按颜色分开，精心操作的膜可以分离，却要消耗功，并在别处产生影响。摩擦也把有序运动变成分散分子运动。恢复每项微观关联需要不可能的控制。即使底层微观定律常可逆，宏观不可逆仍从统计、关联丢失与约束中出现。\n\n奈拉拒绝只把这个量定义为混乱。一副洗乱的牌看似杂乱，却不因此成为热力学系统，晶体也仍有热状态。经典热力学用可逆热传递除以温度帮助定义变化；统计力学则以兼容微观状态数的对数，把同一量连接到概率。增长定律针对孤立系统，开放系统可以把它输出，并通过消耗自由能建造局部结构。\n\n冰窖展示的是熵：一种与能量分散相关的热力学状态函数，在统计意义上又联系兼容某宏观状态的微观构型数。宏观孤立系统在热力学描述下总熵不会减少，自发过程趋向压倒性更可能的宏观状态，微小系统则可能出现涨落。若别处出现更大增加，局部下降可以发生，如制冷机与生命系统。能量守恒解释没有任何东西消失，熵则解释冷为何不会自行回家，恢复昨天的排列。",
    "explanation": "Entropy is a thermodynamic state function related to energy dispersal and, in statistical mechanics, to the number of microscopic configurations compatible with a macrostate. In the macroscopic thermodynamic description, total entropy does not decrease in an isolated system.\n\nThe second law is statistical and does not forbid local decreases. Refrigerators, organisms, and other open systems can build local order by using free energy and producing a compensating or larger entropy increase in their surroundings.",
    "explanationZh": "熵是与能量分散相关的热力学状态函数，在统计力学中又联系兼容某宏观状态的微观构型数。在宏观热力学描述下，孤立系统总熵不会减少。\n\n热力学第二定律具有统计意义，并不禁止局部下降。制冷机、生命体等开放系统可以利用自由能建立局部有序，同时在环境中产生补偿性或更大的熵增加。"
