    "explanation": "The field concept assigns a physical quantity to every point in space and time. Fields may be scalar, vector, or more complex; sources shape them, and objects respond according to properties that couple to them.\n\nFields are more than bookkeeping for distant forces: they can store and transfer energy and momentum and propagate disturbances at finite speed. A measured force depends on both the field and the particular test object.",
    "explanationZh": "场概念把物理量分配到时空中的每一点。场可以是标量、向量或更复杂对象；源塑造场，物体则按与场耦合的自身性质作出响应。\n\n场不只是远距作用的记账工具：它可以储存并传递能量与动量，也能以有限速度传播扰动。测得的力同时取决于场与特定测试物体。"
