    "explanation": "Mathematical induction proves a proposition over a discrete ordered domain by establishing a base case and a universal inductive step from an arbitrary case to its successor. These together cover every index reachable from the base.\n\nChecking examples is not induction, and neither part can be omitted. Strong induction allows all earlier cases in the hypothesis, while the claimed domain and starting index must be stated correctly.",
    "explanationZh": "数学归纳法通过证明基础情形，并证明任意情形到其后继的普遍传递，在离散有序定义域上确立命题。两者合在一起覆盖从基础可到达的每个索引。\n\n检查样例不是归纳，两部分也都不能省略。强归纳允许在假设中使用此前所有情形，而命题的定义域与起始索引必须准确说明。"
