    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "At Grey Cape, severe storms occurred on about one night in ten. A new bell rang on eight of every ten storm nights, and on two of every ten calm nights. When it rang, keeper Lio announced an 80 percent chance of storm because the bell was right eight times in ten during storms. Harbourmaster Nara asked him to imagine one hundred nights before closing the port.\n\nAbout ten of those nights would be stormy and ninety calm. The bell would ring on roughly eight storm nights and eighteen calm nights. Among the twenty-six ringing nights, only about eight would contain storms, making the probability near eight divided by twenty-six, or 31 percent. The bell carried useful evidence, but the rarity of storms supplied many more opportunities for false alarms. One sensitive sensor could still generate many false alarms when the underlying event was rare. Sensitivity alone was not the probability Lio wanted.\n\nNara rewrote the same calculation as odds. Before hearing the bell, storm odds were one to nine. A ring was four times as likely during storm as during calm, so its likelihood ratio was four. Multiplying gave posterior odds of four to nine, again about 31 percent probability. The old belief was not erased by new evidence; it was transformed according to how differently the evidence was expected under competing possibilities.\n\nA sharp pressure fall then arrived. Historical records made that reading three times as likely in storms as in calm weather after accounting for the bell. Multiplying the odds again gave twelve to nine, or about 57 percent. But if the pressure sensor and bell both responded to the same gust pattern, treating them as conditionally independent would count evidence twice. Nara estimated their joint behaviour rather than automatically multiplying separate ratios.\n\nStorm seasons changed the starting rate, and worn equipment changed the likelihoods. Nara updated calibration, stated uncertainty, and compared decisions with their costs: closing unnecessarily harmed trade, while remaining open in a storm risked lives. The probability calculation informed but did not choose the action without a loss function. Evidence order made no difference when the same coherent model and data were used, though model misspecification could produce confident error.\n\nNara was using Bayesian updating: begin with prior probabilities or odds, evaluate the likelihood of observed evidence under competing hypotheses, and combine them to obtain posterior probabilities. In odds form, posterior odds equal prior odds multiplied by a likelihood ratio; dependent evidence requires a joint or conditional model. Priors, likelihoods, and decisions should remain distinguishable and open to revision. Lio had treated the bell as a verdict. Nara treated it as one piece of evidence whose meaning depended on what was plausible before it rang.",
    "storyBodyZh": "灰角每十个夜晚大约有一夜发生严重风暴。新警钟在十个风暴夜里会响八次，在十个平静夜里也会误响两次。钟一响，守望员利奥便宣布风暴概率为八成，因为风暴发生时警钟十次能对八次。港务长娜拉请他先想象一百个夜晚，再决定是否封港。\n\n其中约十夜有风暴，九十夜平静。警钟会在约八个风暴夜和十八个平静夜响起。二十六个响钟夜里，只有约八夜真正有风暴，概率接近八除以二十六，即 31%。警钟提供有用证据，但风暴罕见，平静夜给误报留下更多机会。底层事件罕见时，高灵敏度传感器仍可产生大量误报。灵敏度本身并不是利奥想要的概率。\n\n娜拉把同一计算改写成赔率。听钟前，风暴赔率是一比九。响钟在风暴中出现的可能是平静时的四倍，因此似然比为四。相乘后得到四比九的后验赔率，概率仍约 31%。旧判断没有被新证据抹掉，而是按该证据在竞争可能下出现的差异程度被改写。\n\n随后气压急降。历史记录显示，在已计入警钟后，这个读数出现在风暴中的可能是平静时的三倍。再次相乘得到十二比九，即约 57%。但若气压计与警钟都响应同一种阵风，把它们视为条件独立就会把证据算两次。娜拉估计二者联合表现，而非自动相乘两个独立比率。\n\n风暴季会改变起始发生率，设备磨损会改变似然。娜拉更新校准、说明不确定性，并把决定与代价比较：不必要封港伤害贸易，风暴中开放则危及生命。概率能支持行动，却不能在没有损失函数时替人选择。使用同一连贯模型与数据时，证据顺序不改变结果，模型设错却会制造自信错误。\n\n娜拉使用的是贝叶斯更新：从先验概率或赔率出发，评估观察证据在竞争假设下的似然，再结合成后验概率。赔率形式中，后验赔率等于先验赔率乘似然比；相互依赖的证据需要联合或条件模型。先验、似然与决策应彼此区分，并保持可修订。利奥把警钟当判决，娜拉则把它当成一份证据，其意义取决于钟响以前什么本来更可能。",
    "explanation": "Bayesian updating combines prior probabilities with the likelihood of observed evidence under competing hypotheses to produce posterior probabilities. In odds form, posterior odds equal prior odds multiplied by a likelihood ratio.\n\nBase rates matter, dependent evidence must not be counted as independent, and calibration can change over time. Posterior probabilities inform decisions, but utilities or losses are additionally required to choose actions.",
    "explanationZh": "贝叶斯更新把先验概率与证据在竞争假设下的似然结合，得到后验概率。以赔率表示时，后验赔率等于先验赔率乘以似然比。\n\n基础发生率不可忽略，相互依赖的证据不能按独立信息重复计算，校准也会随时间改变。后验概率支持决策，但选择行动还需要效用或损失。"
