    "explanation": "Hierarchical information organization groups items into nested parent-child containers, creating paths that provide context, navigation, scope, and administrative inheritance.\n\nA hierarchy cannot represent every cross-cutting relationship. Stable identifiers, metadata, tags, search, references, naming conventions, permissions, lifecycle rules, and version control are complementary parts of a usable information system.",
    "explanationZh": "层级化信息组织把项目放入嵌套父子容器，形成能提供情境、导航、范围与管理继承的路径。\n\n层级无法表达所有交叉关系。稳定标识、元数据、标签、搜索、引用、命名规范、权限、生命周期规则与版本控制，是可用信息系统的互补部分。"
