    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Five island harbours shared a cargo ledger. A ship could depart only once, yet fog delayed signal boats. Harbour A recorded departure and sent copies; before acknowledgements returned, its tower lost power. Harbour B saw no entry, elected itself coordinator, and recorded a second departure token. When the fog cleared, two valid-looking histories claimed the same cargo. Fast local action had sacrificed a single shared order.\n\nEngineer Rhea divided time into numbered terms. In each term, a harbour could vote for at most one coordinator. The coordinator appended proposed entries to its log and considered one committed only after acknowledgements from a majority. Any two majorities among five shared at least one harbour, making it harder for conflicting entries at the same position to both become committed. A new coordinator had to carry a sufficiently up-to-date log before receiving votes.\n\nDuring the next outage, two harbours formed one group and three formed another. The pair could not reach a majority, so it stopped confirming departures even though local docks remained usable. The group of three continued after electing a coordinator. Both groups could keep serving stale reads, but only the majority side could safely append a newly committed departure under the chosen consistency rule during partition. Waiting protected agreement but reduced availability for the minority partition. Rhea refused to label silence a failure of the protocol; under uncertain delay and partition, sometimes no safe progress could be guaranteed until communication improved.\n\nA coordinator crashed after sending an entry to two followers but before announcing commitment. The next coordinator retained the surviving entry but did not mark it committed merely because an old-term entry appeared on a majority. It first followed the protocol's current-term commitment rule, which established a safe prefix containing that entry, and only then exposed the departure as durable. Clients retried timed-out requests, so commands carried unique identifiers and were processed idempotently. Receiving, appending, committing, applying, and replying were distinct states; treating any one as the others recreated duplicate departures.\n\nThe design assumed harbours might stop or lose messages, not forge arbitrary votes. Defending against malicious participants required different quorum sizes, signatures, and protocols. Clock synchronisation could improve performance but could not replace the ordering rules. Membership changes were themselves committed decisions because changing the voters carelessly could create two disjoint majorities. Safety and progress depended on an explicit fault model.\n\nThe islands had built distributed consensus: multiple nodes agree on one value or ordered log despite failures and message delay, preserving safety so conflicting decisions are not both committed while seeking liveness when conditions permit. Leaders, terms, quorum intersection, replicated logs, and durable commitment are common mechanisms under crash-fault assumptions. Network partitions force trade-offs, and retries require idempotency. The ship had not physically departed twice. Two coordinators had each mistaken a local record for a decision shared by the system.",
    "storyBodyZh": "五座岛港共享一份货运账。每艘船只能离港一次，浓雾却会拖延信号船。A 港记录离港并发送副本，确认返回前灯塔断电。B 港看不见该记录，推选自己为协调者，又登记一枚离港令牌。雾散以后，两段看似有效的历史都声称拥有同一批货。快速本地行动牺牲了单一共享顺序。\n\n工程师蕾娅把时间划成编号任期。每个任期里，一座港口最多投票给一名协调者。协调者把提议条目追加到日志，只有得到多数确认后才视为提交。五港中任意两个多数至少共享一港，使同一位置的冲突条目更难同时提交。新协调者还必须携带足够新的日志，才可获得选票。\n\n下一次中断时，两港组成一组，三港组成另一组。两港无法取得多数，即使本地码头可用，也停止确认离港；三港组则选出协调者后继续。两组都可继续提供旧读取，但按所选一致性规则，分区期间只有多数侧能安全追加新提交离港。等待保护一致，却降低少数分区的可用性。蕾娅拒绝把沉默称为协议失败：在延迟与分区不确定时，有时必须等通信改善，才能保证安全推进。\n\n一名协调者把条目发给两名跟随者后崩溃，尚未宣布提交。下一任协调者保留存活条目，却没有因为旧任期条目出现在多数节点就直接宣布提交；它先按协议完成当前任期的提交规则，确立包含该条目的安全日志前缀，才对外显示离港已持久。客户端会重试超时请求，因此命令带唯一标识，并按幂等方式处理。接收、追加、提交、应用与回复是不同状态；把其中任一个当成其他状态，就会重造重复离港。\n\n这套设计假设港口可能停机或丢消息，不假设它们伪造任意选票。防御恶意参与者需要不同的 quorum 大小、签名与协议。时钟同步可改善性能，却不能替代排序规则。成员变更本身也要作为决定提交，因为随意改变投票者可能制造两个互不相交的多数。安全与推进取决于明确故障模型。\n\n群岛建立的是分布式共识：多个节点在故障与消息延迟中，对一个值或有序日志达成一致；它要保持安全性，不让冲突决定同时提交，也在条件允许时追求活性。领导者、任期、quorum 交叠、复制日志与持久提交，是崩溃故障假设下的常见机制。网络分区迫使系统取舍，重试则要求幂等。船并未真正离港两次，只是两名协调者都把本地记录误当成全系统共享的决定。",
    "explanation": "Distributed consensus lets multiple nodes agree on a value or ordered log despite failures and message delay. Safety prevents conflicting commitments; liveness seeks eventual progress when the fault and communication assumptions permit it.\n\nLeader terms, intersecting quorums, replicated logs, and explicit commitment rules are common mechanisms for crash faults. Exact commitment rules differ by protocol, so majority replication alone is not a universal test. Partitions create availability trade-offs, while malicious faults, retries, and membership changes require additional design.",
    "explanationZh": "分布式共识让多个节点在故障与消息延迟下，对一个值或有序日志达成一致。安全性阻止冲突提交，活性则在故障与通信假设允许时追求最终推进。\n\n领导任期、交叠 quorum、复制日志与明确提交规则是处理崩溃故障的常见机制。具体提交规则随协议而异，因此复制到多数并非普遍充分条件。分区带来可用性取舍，恶意故障、重试与成员变更还需要额外设计。"
