    "explanation": "Energy efficiency relates a defined useful service or output to the energy input required under stated boundaries and operating conditions. Unwanted heat, friction, auxiliary demand, transport, and cycling can reduce it without violating conservation.\n\nMetrics differ across technologies, such as boiler efficiency and heat-pump coefficient of performance. Higher efficiency can lower energy per service while total consumption still depends on service demand and rebound.",
