    "storyBody": "Farmer Daro celebrated every cart of grain leaving his valley. He also sold the straw and moved manure from the dairy yard to a distant buyer. For several seasons the soil still looked dark, yet yields gradually fell and pale leaves appeared first on the far field. Daro blamed tired seed. Agronomist Sera placed the grain, straw, milk, manure, rain, dust, feed, fertiliser, runoff, and soil tests on one ledger. The farm had counted money crossing its gate and ignored elements crossing with it.\n\nSera treated the soil as changing stocks rather than an inexhaustible container. Nitrogen, phosphorus, potassium, sulfur, and other elements entered in different forms, moved through plants, animals, microbes, water, and organic matter, then left in products, gases, erosion, drainage, or waste. Energy flowed through sunlight and heat; chemical elements could be reused but were also exported or dispersed. A balanced annual total still concealed a depleted hilltop and an overloaded yard.\n\nThe first response spread more nitrogen everywhere. Rain soon carried nitrate below shallow roots, and wet compacted patches released nitrogen gases. Phosphorus accumulated near the barn while remaining less available in other soils because chemistry and erosion controlled its movement. Sera distinguished total content from plant-available form and matched source, rate, timing, and placement to crop demand, weather, soil, and realistic yield. More input at the wrong place or time increased loss without feeding the plant.\n\nDaro began returning crop residues, composting suitable manure, growing legumes, rotating deep- and shallow-rooted crops, and protecting soil from erosion. These practices did not create every element from nothing. Legumes brought biologically fixed atmospheric nitrogen into the farm system but still required other nutrients; manure redistributed nutrients originally taken from feed and land. Composting, storage, and application could lose nitrogen or introduce pathogens, salts, contaminants, and runoff if poorly managed.\n\nSera used repeated soil and tissue tests, yield maps, nutrient budgets, field history, and observations of water and soil structure. She accounted for uncertainty and delayed release from organic pools. The goal was neither mining fertility nor forcing every input to remain on the farm. Excess nutrients could damage water, air, climate, animal health, and crop quality. Efficient production meant retaining useful flows, replacing unavoidable exports, and preventing harmful accumulation or escape.\n\nThe valley learned nutrient cycling: the movement, transformation, storage, reuse, and loss of essential elements through soil, organisms, water, air, products, and management. Harvest and animal products remove nutrients; weathering, fixation, feed, fertiliser, residues, manure, deposition, and biological processes add or redistribute them. Availability depends on form, place, timing, biology, and conditions, not only total quantity. Daro's harvests had never vanished. Each cart carried part of the farm away, and the ledger finally showed which parts needed a safe route home.",
    "storyBodyZh": "农夫达罗为每一车驶出山谷的谷物庆祝。他还卖掉秸秆，又把奶牛场粪肥运给远方买家。几个季节里，土壤仍显得黝黑，产量却慢慢下降，远处田块先出现苍白叶片。达罗责怪种子疲惫。农艺师塞拉把谷物、秸秆、牛奶、粪肥、雨、尘、饲料、肥料、径流与土壤检测放进同一本账。农场只数过穿越大门的钱，没有数随之穿越的元素。\n\n塞拉把土壤看成变化的储库，而非取之不尽的容器。氮、磷、钾、硫与其他元素以不同形态进入，经植物、动物、微生物、水和有机质移动，再通过产品、气体、侵蚀、排水或废物离开。能量随阳光与热流动，化学元素可以再利用，也会被运走或分散。全场年度总量平衡，仍可能掩盖山顶耗竭与畜栏旁过量。\n\n第一项反应是在所有地方增加氮肥。雨水很快把硝酸盐带到浅根以下，潮湿压实地块又释放含氮气体。磷在牛舍旁累积，在其他土中却因化学与侵蚀控制而较难利用。塞拉区分总含量与植物可用形态，再按作物需求、天气、土壤与现实目标产量匹配来源、用量、时间与位置。错误地点或时间的更多投入，只会增加流失，不会喂饱植物。\n\n达罗开始归还作物残体，妥善堆肥，种植豆科，轮作深浅根作物，并保护土壤免受侵蚀。这些做法并不会凭空创造每种元素。豆科把生物固定的空气氮带入农场，仍需其他养分；粪肥只是重新分配原本来自饲料与土地的养分。若管理不当，堆制、储存与施用会损失氮，也可能引入病原、盐分、污染物和径流。\n\n塞拉反复使用土壤与植株检测、产量地图、养分预算、田块历史，并观察水与土壤结构。她考虑不确定性，以及有机库迟缓释放。目标既不是开采肥力，也不是强迫每份投入永远留在农场。过量养分会伤害水、空气、气候、动物健康与作物质量。高效生产要保留有用流动，补回无法避免的输出，并防止有害累积或逃逸。\n\n山谷学会的是养分循环：必需元素在土壤、生物、水、空气、产品与管理之间的移动、转化、储存、再利用与损失。收成与动物产品会带走养分，风化、固定、饲料、肥料、残体、粪肥、沉降与生物过程会添加或重分配它们。可利用程度取决于形态、地点、时间、生物与条件，而非只有总量。达罗的收成从未消失，每辆车都带走农场的一部分，账本终于显示哪些部分需要一条安全回家路。",
    "explanation": "Nutrient cycling is the movement, transformation, storage, reuse, and loss of essential elements through soil, organisms, water, air, products, and management.\n\nInputs, harvest exports, animal flows, chemical form, microbial processes, timing, placement, erosion, drainage, and gaseous losses determine availability and environmental impact. Balancing one total can hide local depletion or accumulation.",
    "explanationZh": "养分循环是必需元素在土壤、生物、水、空气、产品与管理之间的移动、转化、储存、再利用与损失。\n\n投入、收成输出、动物流动、化学形态、微生物过程、时间、位置、侵蚀、排水与气态损失共同决定可利用性和环境影响。一个总量平衡可掩盖局部耗竭或累积。"
