    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Farmer Pela showed the inspector a cow with a full trough, clean coat, normal temperature, and no visible wound. By her checklist, the animal lacked nothing. Every afternoon, however, the cow paced the same six steps and struck the gate until the hinge bent. Pela replaced the hinge twice and called the behaviour stubbornness. Veterinarian Sera watched when it began, what preceded it, and what changed when the herd moved outside.\n\nSera first checked nutrition: access, quantity, quality, balance, competition, thirst, and feeding pattern rather than the presence of feed alone. She examined the physical environment for heat, cold, flooring, mud, air, light, space, noise, and resting comfort. She assessed health through injury, disease, pain, function, body condition, and subclinical problems. A normal temperature did not rule out lameness or chronic discomfort.\n\nThe fourth area concerned behavioural interactions with the environment, other animals, and people. Could the cow move, rest, explore, groom, avoid aggression, maintain preferred social contact, and exercise meaningful choice within safe limits? The gate striking began when a dominant animal blocked the only route to water after milking. Outside, several routes and more space allowed avoidance. Sera changed group composition, access points, flooring, timing, and staff handling, then observed whether behaviour and resource use changed.\n\nNone of the first four areas was the animal's mental state itself. They supplied evidence from which likely negative and positive experiences could be cautiously inferred: thirst, pain, fear, frustration, breathlessness, comfort, interest, security, pleasure, or social connection. Sera combined behaviour, physiology, health, preference and motivation tests, context, and repeated observation. Preference showed what an animal chose under test conditions, while motivation tests helped indicate how hard it would work for access; neither measure stood alone. Positive signs required genuine opportunity, not coercion. She did not claim direct access to the cow's thoughts or explain every repetitive action with one emotion.\n\nAfter the changes, gate striking declined and resting, exploration, and affiliative contact increased. Pela learned that removing obvious suffering was not the full aim; animals could also have opportunities for positive engagement and agency. Domains interacted: heat altered drinking and behaviour, pain changed social contact, and crowding affected rest. Assessments remained individual and time-specific, supported decisions, and triggered investigation rather than producing one eternal welfare score.\n\nThe cow was assessed with the Five Domains model of animal welfare: nutrition, physical environment, health, and behavioural interactions provide evidence used to infer the animal's overall mental experiences. The model considers negative and positive states and how interacting conditions affect welfare over time. It is a structured assessment framework, not mind reading or a substitute for species-specific expertise. Pela's first checklist proved that the cow was alive, fed, and visibly unbroken. The bent hinge revealed what those facts had not yet asked about living.",
    "storyBodyZh": "农场主佩拉向检查员展示一头食槽充足、皮毛干净、体温正常且没有可见伤口的奶牛。按她的清单，动物什么都不缺。可每天下午，奶牛都会沿同样六步来回走动，再撞击栏门直到铰链弯曲。佩拉换过两次铰链，把行为归为固执。兽医塞拉则观察它何时开始、之前发生什么，以及牛群移到户外后有什么改变。\n\n塞拉先检查营养：不只看有无饲料，还看取得、数量、质量、平衡、竞争、口渴与进食节奏。她检查物理环境中的热、冷、地面、泥、水、空气、光、空间、噪声与休息舒适，并从伤害、疾病、疼痛、功能、体况与亚临床问题评估健康。体温正常并不能排除跛行或慢性不适。\n\n第四个领域关注奶牛与环境、其他动物及人的行为互动。奶牛能否移动、休息、探索、梳理、避开攻击、维持偏好社交，并在安全界限内作出有意义选择？撞门始于挤奶后，一头优势牛堵住唯一饮水路线。到了户外，多条路线与更大空间允许回避。塞拉改变分组、入口、地面、时序与人员操作，再观察行为和资源使用是否变化。\n\n前四个领域都不是动物心理状态本身，而是用来谨慎推断可能负面与正面体验的证据：口渴、疼痛、恐惧、挫败、呼吸困难、舒适、兴趣、安全、愉悦或社交连接。塞拉结合行为、生理、健康、偏好与动机测试、情境及重复观察。偏好显示动物在测试条件下选择什么，动机测试帮助判断它愿为取得资源付出多少；二者都不能单独作答。积极迹象还需要真实机会，而非强迫。她不声称直接进入奶牛思想，也不把每项重复行为都归给一种情绪。\n\n调整后，撞门减少，休息、探索与友好接触增加。佩拉明白，移除明显痛苦不是全部目标；动物还可以拥有积极参与与能动机会。各领域相互作用：热改变饮水与行为，疼痛改变社交，拥挤影响休息。评估依个体与时间而定，用来支持决定并触发调查，而非制造一个永恒福利分数。\n\n这头奶牛使用的是动物福利五域模型：营养、物理环境、健康与行为互动提供证据，用来推断动物总体心理体验。模型同时考虑负面与正面状态，以及相互作用的条件怎样跨时间影响福利。它是结构化评估框架，不是读心，也不取代物种专门知识。佩拉第一张清单证明奶牛活着、吃饱、外观未损；弯曲铰链则暴露这些事实尚未追问的生活。",
    "explanation": "The Five Domains model of animal welfare uses evidence from nutrition, physical environment, health, and behavioural interactions to infer an animal's overall mental experiences.\n\nIt considers negative and positive states, interactions among domains, individual variation, and change over time. It structures assessment but does not provide direct access to an animal's thoughts or replace species-specific expertise.",
    "explanationZh": "动物福利五域模型使用营养、物理环境、健康与行为互动的证据，推断动物总体心理体验。\n\n它考虑负面与正面状态、领域间互动、个体差异与时间变化。它组织评估，却不能直接读取动物思想，也不取代物种专门知识。"
