    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Courier Vale delivered a silver message each dusk to quiet the city's racing bells. For months the dose arrived, did its work, and left through the west gate. Then Courier Orra began carrying a separate order to stop mould in the granaries. Each order had served other cities well. Within three evenings, however, Vale's silver messages crowded the streets, the bells slowed too far, and the gate guards could barely stay awake. The mayor blamed a defective batch, because neither courier had ever caused such trouble alone.\n\nArchivist Sen placed both route maps on one table. Orra's order occupied the mill that normally transformed Vale's silver seal before departure, and it slowed the transporter at the west gate. Vale's message therefore remained longer and rose to a higher level despite an unchanged delivery. In another district, two orders left by separate gates yet both commanded guards to become drowsy; their effects added at the same target. A third pair pushed in opposite directions and reduced one another's visible result. Shared timing did not imply one single mechanism.\n\nThe mayor proposed banning every pair of couriers. Sen refused. Some combinations had no meaningful effect, some were intentionally coordinated, and some could be managed by choosing another route, changing timing, adjusting a regimen, or monitoring a relevant outcome under qualified supervision. Severity depended on dose, duration, pathway, therapeutic margin, the citizen's organ function and genetics, and the presence of more messages than the mayor remembered to list. A theoretical route conflict was a reason to investigate, not automatic proof of clinical harm.\n\nTheir first investigation failed because the official ledger contained only orders issued by the palace. The sleepy guard had also bought a night tonic, used a neighbour's pain draught, and started a concentrated botanical extract whose label said only natural strength. Sen performed a complete reconciliation: prescribed and non-prescribed medicines, supplements, herbs, alcohol or other relevant substances, recent starts and stops, formulation, dose, timing, and actual use. The missing lines explained why a previously stable arrangement had changed.\n\nSen warned the council against solving the case by abruptly cancelling a courier from a public list. Stopping or altering an essential order could itself cause harm, and interaction resources differed in evidence, population, and intended use. She checked current product information and trusted professional guidance, assessed symptoms and urgency, contacted the responsible clinicians and pharmacist, and documented a shared plan. When severe new symptoms appeared, the city used its emergency route rather than waiting for an archive debate.\n\nThe crowded streets revealed drug interactions: one medicine or substance can alter another's exposure through absorption, distribution, metabolism, transport, or excretion, or alter its effect through additive, opposing, or otherwise changed action at physiological targets. Not every co-administration is harmful, and risk is specific to the agents, person, purpose, evidence, and management. The mayor had inspected two couriers separately and declared each trustworthy. Sen discovered that safety also belonged to the gate they shared and the guard who received both messages.",
    "storyBodyZh": "信使维尔每天黄昏送来一封银色命令，让城市疾驰的钟声平静。数月里，命令按时抵达、发挥作用，再从西门离开。后来，信使奥拉开始携带另一道命令，阻止粮仓发霉。两道命令在别的城市各自都很可靠，可三个夜晚后，维尔的银色信件挤满街道，钟声慢得过头，守门人困得几乎站不住。市长认定某一批信件有缺陷，因为两名信使单独行动时从未惹出这种麻烦。\n\n档案师森把两张路线图铺在同一张桌上。奥拉的命令占用了平时负责改造维尔银印的磨坊，也拖慢西门的运输者。于是维尔送达量没有改变，命令却停留更久、累积更高。另一城区里，两道命令经不同城门离开，却都要求守卫困倦，作用便在同一目标上相加。还有一对命令方向相反，彼此削弱可见结果。共同出现的时间并不说明只有一种机制。\n\n市长提议禁止所有信使结伴。森拒绝了。有些组合没有重要影响，有些本就为协同而设，另一些可以在专业监督下通过改换路线、调整时机或方案、监测相关结果来管理。严重程度取决于剂量、持续时间、通路、治疗余地、市民的器官功能与遗传，也取决于市长忘记登记的其他命令。一项理论上的路线冲突值得调查，却不自动证明已经造成临床伤害。\n\n第一次调查失败了，因为官方账册只记着宫廷签发的命令。那名困倦守卫还买过夜间补剂，用了邻居的止痛药水，又开始服用标签只写“天然强效”的浓缩植物提取物。森进行完整用药核对：处方与非处方药、补充剂、草药、酒精或其他相关物质、近期开始和停止的项目、剂型、剂量、时机及实际使用方式。那些缺失的行，解释了原本稳定的安排为何改变。\n\n森提醒议事会，不能照着一张公开清单骤然取消某名信使。突然停止或改变必要药物本身就可能造成伤害，不同相互作用资料库的证据、人群与用途也不相同。她核对最新产品信息和可信专业指引，评估症状与紧迫性，联系负责的临床人员和药师，并记录共同方案。出现严重新症状时，城市会启动紧急通道，而不是等待档案争论结束。\n\n拥挤街道揭示的是药物相互作用：一种药物或物质可以通过吸收、分布、代谢、转运或排泄改变另一种药物的暴露，也可以在生理目标上以相加、相反或其他方式改变其作用。并非所有共同使用都会有害，风险取决于具体物质、个体、目的、证据与管理。市长把两名信使分开检查，便宣布各自可靠；森却发现，安全也存在于他们共享的城门，以及同时收到两封命令的守卫身上。",
    "explanation": "Drug interactions occur when one medicine or substance changes another's exposure or effect through pharmacokinetic or pharmacodynamic mechanisms.\n\nTheir importance varies by agent, dose, timing, person, indication, evidence, and monitoring. Medication changes should be based on complete reconciliation and qualified advice, not an isolated public interaction list.",
    "explanationZh": "药物相互作用是指一种药物或物质通过药代动力学或药效动力学机制，改变另一种药物的暴露或作用。\n\n其重要性随物质、剂量、时机、个体、用途、证据与监测而变。用药改变应建立在完整核对与合格专业意见上，而不是孤立的公开相互作用清单。"
