    "storyBody": "Three valleys drew water from Saint Rowan's Spring and each declared it a certain cure for winter fever. In East Vale, the mayor displayed twelve grateful letters. In North Vale, the healer counted everyone who drank after arriving ill and found that most were well a week later. In West Vale, families who chose the spring recovered faster than families who did not. When a fourth village asked whether to build an expensive aqueduct, all three reports reached the council stamped PROOF, although they had not asked or answered the same question.\n\nScholar Meira began with the letters. They showed that improvement was possible and revealed experiences worth investigating, but not how many people failed, recovered without water, received other care, or were selected for display. North Vale had a larger series, yet fever often resolved with time and the sickest residents sometimes went elsewhere. West Vale had a comparison, but spring users were wealthier, lived nearer the clinic, and sought help earlier. More pages reduced neither selection nor confounding by themselves.\n\nMeira organised a prospective trial in which eligible volunteers were assigned by chance to credible alternatives, allocation was concealed, outcomes were defined beforehand, and follow-up included harms. Random assignment balanced known and unknown differences on average; blinding reduced some changes in behaviour and measurement where it was feasible. The spring group did no better on the chosen outcome. The mayors called the trial superior by ritual alone, until Meira showed missing participants, a wide uncertainty interval, and a preparation unlike the one commonly used.\n\nA later, larger trial corrected those weaknesses, while several independent teams reported similar results. Meira synthesised them systematically rather than choosing the most dramatic study. Even then, she examined risk of bias, inconsistency, indirectness, imprecision, and missing negative findings. Study design offered a starting point for judging causal claims, not an automatic seal of truth. One meticulous observation could expose an unexpected danger; one poorly conducted randomised trial could still mislead.\n\nThe council then asked whether rare liver injury appeared after ten years. Meira did not demand an impossibly vast decade-long trial before listening. Registries, pharmacovigilance, mechanistic evidence, case reports, and well-designed observational studies could be crucial for rare or delayed harms. Diagnostic accuracy, prognosis, lived experience, prevalence, and intervention benefit each required fitting evidence and methods. Ethical and practical limits also mattered. The strongest available answer was the one best matched to the question and least damaged by avoidable bias, not always the same rung on a rigid ladder.\n\nThe valleys learned the hierarchy of evidence: a structured way to give different study designs and bodies of evidence different initial weight, then judge how directly and reliably they answer a specific question. Randomised controlled evidence is often powerful for intervention causality, but certainty also depends on conduct, consistency, precision, directness, reporting, and the total evidence; other designs may be indispensable for harms and other questions. Certainty about an effect was not itself a recommendation: benefits, harms, values, equity, feasibility, and resources still entered the aqueduct decision. The stamp PROOF disappeared. Meira wrote what was known, how it was known, and what uncertainty remained.",
    "storyBodyZh": "三个山谷都从圣罗文泉取水，也都宣布它是冬季发热的确定疗法。东谷市长展示十二封感谢信；北谷疗愈师统计所有患病后喝水的人，发现一周后大多康复；西谷则发现自愿选择泉水的家庭恢复得比未选择者更快。第四个村庄询问是否应修一条昂贵水渠时，三份报告都盖着“证明”送进议事会，尽管它们提出和回答的并不是同一个问题。\n\n学者梅拉先看感谢信。它们说明改善可能发生，也显出值得调查的体验，却没有告诉她多少人失败、多少人不喝水也会恢复、谁还接受其他照护，以及哪些来信被挑出来展示。北谷病例更多，但发热本会随时间消退，最重者有时去了别处。西谷有比较组，可饮泉水者更富裕、离诊所更近，也更早求助。页面增多本身并不会减少选择偏差或混杂。\n\n梅拉组织一项前瞻试验，把符合条件且同意参加的人随机分到可信替代方案，隐藏分配，预先规定结局，并在随访中记录伤害。随机分配会在平均意义上平衡已知与未知差异；可行时的盲法能减少某些行为与测量变化。泉水组在选定结局上并不更好。市长们正想仅凭仪式把试验奉为最高证据，梅拉却指出失访、很宽的不确定区间，以及所用制剂与日常版本并不相同。\n\n后来一项更大的试验修正这些弱点，几个独立团队也报告相似结果。梅拉系统综合它们，而不是挑选最戏剧性的研究。即便如此，她仍检查偏倚风险、不一致、间接性、不精确与未发表的负面发现。研究设计只是判断因果主张的起点，不是自动真理印章。一项严谨观察可能发现意外危险，一项执行糟糕的随机试验仍然可能误导。\n\n议事会接着问，十年后是否会出现罕见肝损伤。梅拉没有在倾听前强求一项几乎不可能的大型十年试验。登记资料、药物警戒、机制证据、病例报告与设计良好的观察研究，对罕见或延迟伤害可能至关重要。诊断准确性、预后、生活体验、流行程度和干预获益各自需要匹配的证据与方法，伦理和实践限制也必须考虑。最强答案是最贴合问题、最少受可避免偏倚损害的答案，并不永远来自僵硬梯子的同一级。\n\n三个山谷学会的是证据层级：先按不同研究设计与证据总体赋予不同起始权重，再判断它们能以多直接、多可靠的方式回答具体问题。随机对照证据常对干预因果很有力，但确定性还取决于执行、相互一致、精确度、直接性、报告与全部证据；伤害及其他问题又可能离不开别种设计。对效应的确定性本身还不是建议，修建水渠仍要衡量获益、伤害、价值、公平、可行性与资源。“证明”印章被撤下，梅拉改写清楚我们知道什么、如何知道，以及还剩多少不确定。",
    "explanation": "A hierarchy of evidence gives study designs different initial weight according to the question and their ability to limit bias and support inference.\n\nIt is not a rigid universal pyramid. Certainty also depends on study conduct, consistency, precision, directness, reporting, and the whole evidence base; different questions may require different designs.",
