    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Royal gardener Toma took a carefully adjusted palace medicine that kept the rhythm of his heart-work steady. At the autumn fair, a seller offered concentrated moonroot for sleep and assured him that plants could not interfere with manufactured bottles. Toma omitted it from the clinic ledger because he did not regard tea, powder, and tincture as medicines. Two weeks later his measurements shifted and bruises appeared along his arms. Physician Eda increased the palace dose, not knowing that a second active preparation had already entered the same body.\n\nPharmacist Ro noticed dried purple sediment in Toma's cup and reopened the history without accusation. The extract contained multiple constituents whose amount varied with species, plant part, harvest, processing, storage, and concentration. A leaf eaten as food was not necessarily equivalent to an extract distilled into drops. Labels could be incomplete; substitution, contamination, and inconsistent strength complicated prediction. Natural origin described where a substance came from, not whether it lacked pharmacological action, toxicity, or quality problems.\n\nRo traced several possible crossings. A constituent might inhibit or induce an enzyme or transporter, changing how quickly the palace medicine was absorbed, transformed, or cleared. Another might act on the same physiological system, adding to or opposing its effect without changing blood concentration. Food, alcohol, supplements, smoking, illness, organ function, genetics, dose, timing, and duration could alter the result. Some changes appeared quickly; enzyme induction or cumulative effects could take longer and persist after the last cup.\n\nThe court demanded a permanent blacklist of all roots. Ro resisted. For many products, evidence came from laboratory findings, case reports, small studies, or variable preparations; a plausible mechanism did not always become a meaningful effect in every person. Conversely, absence from a warning list did not prove safety. She checked the exact product and purpose, current authoritative resources, known and uncertain risks, Toma's symptoms and measurements, and whether a safer alternative or monitoring plan existed.\n\nEda nearly told Toma to stop both preparations immediately. Ro paused her. Abruptly changing an essential medicine or a regularly used active product could create new harm, and the right response depended on urgency. They arranged prompt qualified review, documented every prescribed and non-prescribed substance, and agreed on one coordinated plan. Toma learned to bring bottles, photographs, doses, and timing to every appointment. Severe symptoms would trigger urgent care, not an experiment conducted alone at home.\n\nThe missing root revealed herb-drug interactions: herbal products can change a medicine's exposure through absorption, metabolism, transport, or elimination, or change its effect through additive or opposing physiological action. Risk depends on the exact product, strength, dose, person, medicine, timing, evidence, and management; uncertainty is often substantial. The palace medicine had not suddenly become unreliable in isolation. The ledger had drawn an artificial border around one cabinet while two biologically active preparations were already meeting beyond it.",
    "storyBodyZh": "皇家园丁托马服用一种经过仔细调整的宫廷药物，让心脏工作的节律保持平稳。秋季集市上，一名商贩出售帮助睡眠的浓缩月根，保证植物绝不会干扰人工药瓶。托马没有把它写进诊所账册，因为他不把茶、粉末和酊剂当成药物。两周后，他的测量结果发生变化，手臂也出现瘀斑。医生埃达不知道另一种活性制剂已经进入同一身体，反而增加了宫廷药物的量。\n\n药师洛在托马杯底看见紫色沉淀，便不带指责地重新询问。提取物含有多种成分，其含量会随物种、植物部位、采收、加工、储存与浓缩程度而变。作为食物吃下一片叶，与把它浓缩成滴剂并不必然相同。标签可能不完整，替代、污染和强度不一致也使预测更难。“天然”只说明物质来自哪里，并不表示它没有药理作用、毒性或质量问题。\n\n洛追踪几种可能交叉。一种成分可能抑制或诱导某种酶或转运体，改变宫廷药物被吸收、转化或清除的速度；另一种成分可能作用于相同生理系统，在不改变血中浓度时叠加或抵消效果。食物、酒精、补充剂、吸烟、疾病、器官功能、遗传、剂量、时机和持续时间也会改变结果。有些变化很快出现，酶诱导或累积作用却可能较慢，最后一杯之后仍会延续。\n\n宫廷要求列出一张永不改变的禁根清单。洛拒绝了。许多产品的证据来自实验室发现、病例报告、小型研究或成分多变的制剂；机制合理并不保证每个人都会出现有临床意义的效果。反过来，没有进入警示清单也不证明安全。她核对具体产品与用途、当前权威资料、已知与不确定风险、托马的症状和测量，以及是否存在更安全替代或监测方案。\n\n埃达差点要求托马立刻停止两种制剂，洛拦住了她。突然改变必要药物或长期使用的活性产品，本身可能制造新伤害，正确回应取决于紧迫性。他们安排及时的专业复核，记录每一种处方与非处方物质，并商定一项协调方案。托马学会每次就诊都带来药瓶、照片、剂量和服用时间；严重症状应触发紧急照护，而不是独自在家试验。\n\n那条缺失记录揭示的是草药与药物相互作用：草药产品可以通过吸收、代谢、转运或清除改变药物暴露，也能通过相加或相反的生理作用改变药效。风险取决于具体产品、强度、剂量、个体、药物、时机、证据与管理，而不确定性往往很大。宫廷药物并非孤立地突然失去可靠性，账册只在人为划定的药柜边界停下，两种具有生物活性的制剂早已在边界之外相遇。",
    "explanation": "Herb-drug interactions occur when a herbal product changes a medicine's exposure or physiological effect.\n\nProduct identity, concentration, quality, dose, timing, individual factors, and evidence all matter. Full medication reconciliation and qualified advice are safer than assuming natural means inert or changing treatment from a generic blacklist.",
    "explanationZh": "草药与药物相互作用是草药产品改变某种药物的暴露或生理作用。\n\n产品身份、浓度、质量、剂量、时机、个体因素与证据都很重要。完整用药核对与合格专业意见，比假定天然即无活性或照通用禁用清单自行改药更安全。"
