    "explanation": "Safeguarding is the organised prevention, identification, reporting, and response to risks of abuse, exploitation, neglect, and other harm.\n\nIt requires safe recruitment, conduct, supervision, accessible reporting, need-to-know confidentiality, child-centred response, and lawful referral. Staff should protect and report, not promise secrecy or conduct amateur investigations.",
