    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Riverbend kept a careful ledger of its teenagers: seven broken windows, eleven late arrivals, four fights, and thirty-two warnings for gathering near the bridge. The council funded a programme called Fix the Youth and invited young people to a lecture on better choices. Only three attended; two left early. Councillor Venn entered their absence as another deficit. When spring floods damaged the bridge, however, sixteen teenagers appeared without invitation to move bicycles, translate warnings for grandparents, and mark where water crossed paths the official map had missed.\n\nPlanner Imani asked why the town recorded every risk but none of those capacities. She met the group in places they already used and invited them to define what a safer riverfront would mean. They identified dark paths, inaccessible notices, a missing evening bus, and a low wall where younger children climbed during high water. Artists, coders, carers, mechanics, quiet observers, and persuasive speakers brought different strengths. Imani did not pretend hardship was absent; she added assets and aspirations to a picture previously made entirely of problems.\n\nThe council's first response was decorative participation. It put two teenagers in a publicity photograph after engineers had completed the plan. The group refused. With adult support, they received a real design brief, budget limits, safety training, transport, accessible meetings, named responsibilities, and authority over defined choices. Engineers retained duties that required professional competence, while young people tested routes, designed multilingual signs, gathered peer evidence, and presented alternatives. Partnership meant neither adult domination nor handing adult liability to minors.\n\nConflict arrived when the young designers chose a night market beside the river. Venn cited the old ledger and proposed cancelling everything. Imani helped them examine lighting, supervision, transport, weather triggers, safeguarding, costs, noise, and emergency closure. The group revised the site and operating plan. Strength-based work did not deny risk or excuse harmful conduct; it combined prevention with opportunities to practise judgement, contribution, connection, and recovery after mistakes.\n\nBy autumn, several participants had learned technical skills, but the deeper change was relational. Each had at least one reliable adult who knew more than an incident number, peers expected useful contribution, and the town had made visible space for their decisions. Outcomes differed and no programme guaranteed a smooth future. Some young people needed specialised services beyond the project. The council tracked belonging, competence, confidence, agency, contribution, safety, and access to opportunity alongside reductions in harm.\n\nRiverbend discovered positive youth development: an intentional, strengths-based approach that engages young people as active partners and supports their assets through opportunities, supportive relationships, participation, skill-building, and enabling environments. It complements risk prevention and targeted services rather than replacing them, and youth need not carry adult burdens to prove leadership. Venn's ledger had accurately counted broken windows. Imani changed the town by counting who could read the river, then giving them the tools and authority to help repair more than glass.",
    "storyBodyZh": "河湾镇认真记录青少年：七扇破窗、十一次迟到、四场打架，以及三十二次因聚集在桥边而收到的警告。议事会资助一项“修好青年”计划，请年轻人来听如何作出更好选择的讲座。只有三人出席，两人提前离开。维恩议员把缺席也记作一项缺陷。然而春洪冲坏桥梁时，十六名青少年不请自来，搬开自行车、为祖辈翻译警报，还标出官方地图遗漏的积水路径。\n\n规划师伊曼妮追问，小镇为何记录每项风险，却不记录这些能力。她在年轻人本来就会去的地方见面，请他们定义更安全的河岸意味着什么。他们指出昏暗小路、无法理解的告示、缺失的夜班公交，以及涨水时幼童会攀爬的矮墙。画家、程序员、照护者、修理者、安静观察者与善于说服的人带来不同优势。伊曼妮没有假装困境不存在，只是在原本全由问题组成的图画里加入资源与愿望。\n\n议事会最初只提供装饰性参与：工程师完成方案后，请两名少年站进宣传照片。小组拒绝了。在成人支持下，他们得到真实设计任务、预算限制、安全培训、交通、可及会议、明确职责，以及对规定范围内选择的决定权。工程师保留需要专业能力的责任，年轻人则测试路线、设计多语标牌、收集同伴证据并提出替代方案。伙伴关系既不是成人支配，也不是把成人责任推给未成年人。\n\n年轻设计者选择在河边办夜市时，冲突到来。维恩翻出旧账册，提议取消全部项目。伊曼妮帮助他们检查照明、监督、交通、天气触发条件、保护、成本、噪声与紧急关闭。小组随后修改地点和运行计划。优势导向并不否认风险，也不为伤害行为开脱；它把预防同练习判断、贡献、联结及犯错后恢复的机会结合起来。\n\n到了秋天，一些参与者学会技术技能，更深的变化却发生在关系里。每个人至少有一名可靠成人知道的不只是事故编号，同伴期待彼此作出有用贡献，小镇也为他们的决定留下可见空间。结果各不相同，没有任何计划能保证未来一路平顺，有些年轻人还需要项目之外的专门服务。议事会在伤害减少以外，也追踪归属、能力、信心、能动性、贡献、安全与机会可及性。\n\n河湾镇发现的是积极青少年发展：一种有意且以优势为基础的方法，把年轻人作为积极伙伴，通过机会、支持性关系、参与、技能培养与有利环境发展他们的资源。它补充而非取代风险预防与针对性服务，年轻人也不必背负成人责任才能证明领导力。维恩的账册准确数出了破窗；伊曼妮先数清谁能读懂河流，再给他们工具与权限，镇子修复的便不再只有玻璃。",
    "explanation": "Positive youth development intentionally builds on young people's strengths through supportive relationships, meaningful opportunities, participation, skill-building, and enabling environments.\n\nIt treats youth as active partners while retaining adult responsibility. It complements prevention and specialised support; it does not deny harm, erase inequality, or require every young person to lead.",
    "explanationZh": "积极青少年发展通过支持性关系、有意义机会、参与、技能培养与有利环境，有意识地发展年轻人的优势。\n\n它把青年视为积极伙伴，同时保留成人责任；它补充预防与专门支持，而不是否认伤害、抹去不平等或要求每个人都承担领导角色。"
