    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Housekeeper Teren prized one blue cloth above all others. It absorbed spills, left no streaks, and survived an entire shift. He began in the washroom, moved through the nursery, polished the dining table, and finished in the kitchen. Every surface looked cleaner after he passed. Two days later, several residents became ill in rooms that had never shared food or close conversation. The manager inspected the gleaming tables and declared hygiene an impossible cause. Teren's cloth hung drying at the centre of the house, spotless to the eye.\n\nInspector Nala marked the cloth with harmless visible dye and repeated its route. Blue traces appeared on handles, taps, toys, chair backs, and a ready-to-eat fruit tray. Hands and gloves then carried the marks farther. Cleaning pressure had not only removed material; the same damp tool had collected it from one zone and deposited part elsewhere. A surface could look free of dirt while still carrying a relevant biological, chemical, or allergenic hazard, and a cloth could become a moving reservoir.\n\nThe manager ordered stronger disinfectant on every object. Nala stopped him from treating product strength as magic. Soil could reduce a disinfectant's performance; the wrong product, concentration, contact, material, or use could create new hazards; and cleaning, sanitising, and disinfecting served different purposes. Labels, ventilation, compatibility, occupational protection, and local procedures mattered. More chemical did not repair a route that continued dipping the same cloth into the same bucket and carrying it across zones.\n\nThey mapped source, carrier, route, destination, and time. High-risk material and ready-to-use areas were separated. Work moved according to a planned clean-to-dirtier sequence where appropriate; cloths and equipment were changed, contained, cleaned, or reprocessed between defined zones; hand and glove practices prevented the worker from becoming another bridge. Food handling, personal care, illness, sharps, laundry, waste, and vulnerable residents required different risk controls rather than one universal colour code.\n\nA week later, the blue dye still appeared on a door. Nala traced it not to Teren's cloth but to a shared spray bottle handled with contaminated gloves. The first fix had focused on the most dramatic object instead of the whole movement system. Training, sufficient supplies, staffing, storage, workflow, reporting, and supervision were revised together. The house followed current public-health, food-safety, product, and workplace guidance suited to its setting rather than copying a hospital routine or household tip without assessment.\n\nThe travelling dye revealed cross-contamination: the unintended transfer of microorganisms, allergens, chemicals, or other hazards from a source to another person, object, surface, or food through contact involving hands, tools, liquids, storage, or workflow. Visible cleanliness does not prove that transfer has been interrupted, and other transmission routes require their own controls. Teren judged each room by how it looked after the cloth arrived. Nala judged the route by what the cloth, the hand, and the bottle carried onward after they left.",
    "storyBodyZh": "家政员特伦最珍爱一块蓝布。它吸水、不留痕，还能撑过整个班次。他从洗手间开始，接着擦婴幼儿房、餐桌，最后进入厨房。每个表面在他离开后都更明亮。两天后，从未共餐、也没有密切交谈的几个房间却有人生病。经理检查闪亮桌面，认定卫生不可能是原因。特伦的布挂在房子中央晾干，肉眼看来一尘不染。\n\n检查员娜拉给布涂上无害可见染料，重走原路线。蓝色痕迹出现在门把、水龙头、玩具、椅背与一盘即食水果上，手和手套又把标记带得更远。擦拭压力不只移除物质；同一块湿布从一个区域收集东西，又把一部分放到别处。表面可以看不见污垢，却仍带有重要的生物、化学或过敏原危险，而一块布也会变成移动储库。\n\n经理命令在每件物品上使用更强消毒剂。娜拉阻止他把产品强度当成魔法。污物可能降低消毒效果，错误产品、浓度、接触、材料或用法会制造新危险，而清洁、卫生处理与消毒承担不同目的。标签、通风、相容性、劳动保护与当地程序都重要。增加化学剂量无法修复一条仍把同一块布放进同一只桶、再带过所有区域的路线。\n\n他们绘出来源、载体、路线、目的地与时间。高风险物质同可直接使用的区域分开；在适用处，工作按计划从较清洁区移向较脏区；布与设备在规定区域之间更换、封存、清洁或再处理；手和手套的做法也防止工作人员变成另一座桥。食品处理、个人照护、疾病、锐器、洗衣、废物和易受影响住民需要不同风险控制，而不是一套通用颜色规则。\n\n一周后，蓝色染料仍出现在一扇门上。娜拉追踪到的不是特伦的布，而是一只被污染手套握过的共用喷瓶。第一次修正只盯着最醒目的物件，没有处理完整移动系统。培训、充足用品、人员配置、储存、工作流、报告与监督因此一同调整。房子依据适合自身场景的最新公共卫生、食品安全、产品与劳动指引行动，而不照搬未经评估的医院流程或家庭窍门。\n\n移动的染料揭示的是交叉污染：微生物、过敏原、化学物或其他危险通过手、工具、液体、储存或工作流程中的接触，从来源非预期地转移到另一人、物体、表面或食物。肉眼干净不能证明转移已经中断，其他传播路线则需要各自的控制。特伦按布到达后房间的样子判断清洁；娜拉按布、手与瓶子离开以后还把什么带向下一处，判断整条路线。",
    "explanation": "Cross-contamination is the unintended movement of microorganisms, allergens, chemicals, or other hazards from one source to another person, surface, object, or food.\n\nTransfer can occur through contact involving hands, tools, cloths, liquids, storage, or workflow. Prevention depends on setting-specific separation, sequencing, cleaning or reprocessing, hand practices, supplies, and current safety guidance.",
    "explanationZh": "交叉污染是微生物、过敏原、化学物或其他危险从一个来源非预期地移动到另一人、表面、物体或食物。\n\n转移可经手、工具、布、液体、储存或工作流程中的接触发生。预防依赖适合场景的分隔、顺序、清洁或再处理、手部做法、用品与当前安全指引。"
