    "explanation": "Colour theory and oxidation explain how starting pigment, added hues, reflected light, fibre condition, and chemical reactions combine to produce a hair-colour result.\n\nOxidative colouring can alter natural melanin and form dye molecules within the fibre. Outcomes vary with the starting material and process, so consultation, testing, product instructions, and safety limits remain essential.",
