    "storyBody": "The Blue Heron Inn gave traveller Sima the wrong room on the night of her examination. The replacement was delayed, her notes were moved without permission, and she arrived at reception furious. Clerk Oren listened without defending the booking system, apologised for the specific failures, found a quiet room, arranged her belongings with consent, covered the added meal, and checked later without demanding praise. Sima returned the next year and recommended the inn more warmly than her companion, whose flawless stay had produced only ordinary satisfaction.\n\nManager Pell called this discovery profitable. He instructed staff to create one small recoverable error for selected guests so that an impressive rescue could manufacture loyalty. A couple given a deliberately late dinner missed their theatre performance. A business traveller recognised the staged apology. A family experiencing its second 'accidental' room error concluded that the inn could not learn. The same recovery gifts now looked like compensation for avoidable disrespect, and trust fell below what a merely adequate stay would have produced.\n\nResearcher Mara separated the first case into perceived justice. Sima had received a useful outcome, a responsive and not needlessly burdensome process, and respectful interpersonal treatment. The remedy matched her actual loss; she had voice; responsibility was acknowledged; speed, explanation, and follow-up were credible. Surprise also reset an expectation that had fallen during a failure. These features could make a successful recovery especially memorable, but they did not erase the original cost or operate like a loyalty machine.\n\nMara compared other cases. Severe or irreversible harm, repeated failures, high prior expectations, obvious organisational control, weak relationships, and inadequate remedies made an uplift less likely. Customers differed in purpose, attribution, history, and preferred response. Some wanted an apology, others immediate correction, information, refund, or assurance that recurrence would be prevented. Results also depended on when satisfaction was measured and what no-failure comparison was used. The apparent uplift was a conditional group pattern, not a promise about every incident.\n\nThe inn stopped practising mistakes and built a recovery system instead. Frontline staff had authority and resources within clear limits; failures were recorded by type and consequence; urgent safety and safeguarding issues followed separate escalation; customers could choose among suitable remedies; and root causes were reviewed. Success meant restoring the customer and reducing recurrence, not merely raising a post-incident score. When recovery could not undo the harm, the inn said so plainly and pursued fair redress rather than theatrical warmth.\n\nSima's return revealed the service recovery paradox: under some conditions, a customer who experiences a failure followed by excellent recovery may report greater satisfaction or loyalty than a customer who experienced no failure. The effect is neither universal nor a reason to create or tolerate errors; severity, repetition, attribution, expectations, relationship, and perceived fairness all matter. Pell tried to bottle the gratitude that followed one honest repair. Mara showed that the only dependable strategy was preventing failure and becoming capable of accountable recovery when prevention failed.",
    "storyBodyZh": "蓝鹭旅店在思玛参加考试前夜给错了房间。更换迟迟未完成，她的笔记也未经允许被移动，于是她愤怒地来到前台。职员奥伦没有替预订系统辩护，而是为具体失误道歉，找到安静房间，在得到同意后整理物品，承担额外餐费，并在稍后复核却不索要赞美。第二年思玛再次入住，向别人推荐旅店时，比同行那位全程无误、却只感到普通满意的朋友更热情。\n\n经理佩尔称这项发现很有利润，命令职员为部分客人制造一个可补救的小错误，再用精彩救援生产忠诚。一对伴侣因刻意延迟的晚餐错过演出，一名商务旅客识破排练过的道歉，一家人第二次遇到“意外”房间错误后认定旅店根本不会学习。同样的补救礼物如今像是为可避免的不尊重付款，信任跌到一次仅仅合格住宿本可达到的水平之下。\n\n研究者玛拉把第一起事件拆成几种被感知的公平。思玛得到实用结果、及时且不过度增加负担的流程，以及尊重的人际对待。补救匹配实际损失，她有表达机会，责任被承认，速度、解释与后续联系也可信。惊喜还重新调整了失误期间下落的期待。这些特征能让成功补救格外难忘，却不会消除原始代价，也不像忠诚机器那样自动工作。\n\n玛拉比较其他案例。伤害严重或不可逆、错误反复、原先期待很高、组织明显可控、关系薄弱和补救不足时，反向提升更不可能发生。顾客的目的、归因、历史和偏好也不同：有人要道歉，有人要立即纠正、信息、退款，或防止重演的保证。结果还取决于何时测量满意，以及使用何种无失误比较基线。所谓提升是有条件的人群模式，不是对每次事件的承诺。\n\n旅店不再练习犯错，转而建立补救系统。一线职员在清楚边界内拥有权限与资源；错误按类型和后果记录；紧急安全与保护问题走不同升级路径；顾客可在合适方案中选择；根本原因也会复核。成功意味着恢复顾客并减少重演，而非只提高事后评分。补救无法撤销伤害时，旅店会坦白说明并寻求公平补偿，而不是表演温暖。\n\n思玛的再次入住揭示的是服务补救悖论：在某些条件下，经历服务失败后又得到出色补救的顾客，可能比从未遇到失败者报告更高满意或忠诚。它并不普遍，更不是制造或容忍错误的理由；严重度、重复、归因、期待、关系与公平感都会影响结果。佩尔想把一次诚实修复后的感激装进瓶子；玛拉证明，可靠策略只有预防失误，并在预防失败时具备负责任的补救能力。",
    "explanation": "The service recovery paradox is the conditional finding that excellent recovery after a failure can sometimes produce higher satisfaction or loyalty than an error-free experience.\n\nIt is not reliable or universal, especially after severe or repeated failures. Fair outcomes, process, respect, attribution, expectations, and history matter; prevention and learning remain preferable to manufactured mistakes.",
