    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Brightwell village received a new protected pump beside the council hall. Engineer Daro tested its flow, posted a health lecture, and expected the old open well to empty. A month later, most morning buckets still came from the well. Daro called residents irrational and printed larger warnings. Investigator Mina arrived before dawn and found the pump locked until office hours, its handle too heavy for several older users, a queue visible from the road, and water with an unfamiliar mineral taste. The technology worked during inspection and failed inside daily life.\n\nMina asked who fetched water, for what purposes, at which times, with what containers, costs, risks, memories, and social expectations. The old well sat beside the route to fields, offered shade and conversation, and could be used without requesting a key. Some households trusted water they had known for generations; others feared being blamed when the new mechanism broke. Knowledge was only one determinant. Capability, physical and social opportunity, motivation, habit, technology, household roles, and wider institutions interacted across levels.\n\nDaro proposed paying people for every pump visit. Use rose while coins lasted and collapsed when payment stopped. A public shaming campaign made some families conceal their source rather than change it. Mina refused to treat behaviour as a button pressed by one message. Incentives, disgust, status, fear, convenience, commitment, and social norms could all influence action, but effects varied and could produce coercion, stigma, gaming, or exclusion. Formative inquiry had to precede the choice of intervention.\n\nResidents helped redesign the service. Opening hours matched water collection, the handle and platform became more accessible, maintenance and spare-part responsibility were public, waiting and drainage improved, and trusted users demonstrated the pump without pretending uncertainty did not exist. Messages connected safe practice to locally meaningful goals and gave practical skills, while households could report taste, function, affordability, harassment, or access problems. The intervention changed environment and service as well as individual intention.\n\nMina measured more than attendance at a launch. She observed correct and sustained use across seasons and groups, pump function, competing sources, unintended consequences, equity, and relevant health or service outcomes. When adoption differed, the team reopened its assumptions instead of blaming a resistant culture. Infrastructure and behaviour supported one another: a broken or inaccessible facility could not be rescued by education, while a technically sound facility could not produce benefit if routines and institutions never made reliable use possible.\n\nThe returning buckets revealed WASH behaviour change: the design and support of sustained water, sanitation, and hygiene practices by addressing interacting contextual, psychosocial, technological, and habitual determinants at individual, household, community, and structural levels. It is not information delivery or infrastructure alone. Daro had installed a pump and expected behaviour to arrive with it. Mina learned that use was another system, built from capability, opportunity, motivation, trust, maintenance, social meaning, and the repeated experience that the pump would still work tomorrow.",
    "storyBodyZh": "亮井村在议事厅旁得到一台受保护的新水泵。工程师达罗测试流量，张贴健康讲座，期待旧露天井从此无人使用。一个月后，大多数清晨水桶仍从旧井提起。达罗称居民不理性，又印出更大的警告。调查者米娜天亮前到场，发现水泵到办公时间才开锁，手柄对几位老人太重，队伍从道路上清晰可见，水还有陌生的矿物味。技术在检查时工作，却在日常生活里失效。\n\n米娜询问谁取水、为了什么、在何时、使用何种容器，并面对哪些成本、风险、记忆与社会期待。旧井位于去田地的路旁，有树荫与交谈，也不必向人借钥匙。一些家庭信任世代熟悉的水，另一些担心新机械损坏时会被责怪。知识只是一个决定因素。能力、物理与社会机会、动机、习惯、技术、家庭角色和更广机构在多个层次相互作用。\n\n达罗提议按每次使用水泵付钱。硬币还在时使用上升，付款结束后立刻回落。公开羞辱又让一些家庭隐瞒水源，而不是改变。米娜拒绝把行为当成一条信息就能按下的按钮。奖励、厌恶、地位、恐惧、便利、承诺与社会规范都可能影响行动，但效果不一，也可能制造强迫、污名、钻空子或排斥。选择干预以前必须先做形成性调查。\n\n居民参与重新设计服务。开放时间匹配取水时段，手柄和平台变得更可及，维护与备件责任公开，等候和排水得到改善，受信任的使用者示范水泵，却不假装没有不确定。信息把安全实践同当地有意义的目标相连，并提供实际技能；家庭也能报告味道、功能、可负担性、骚扰或可及问题。干预改变环境与服务，而不只改变个人意愿。\n\n米娜衡量的不只是启用仪式出席人数。她观察不同季节与人群能否正确持续使用、水泵功能、竞争水源、意外后果、公平，以及相关健康或服务结果。采用情况不同时，团队会重开自身假设，而不责怪某种抗拒文化。基础设施与行为彼此支持：损坏或不可及设施无法靠教育挽救，技术合格的设施若没有日程和机构支持可靠使用，也不会自动产生获益。\n\n重新回到旧井的水桶揭示的是水、环境卫生与个人卫生行为改变：通过处理个人、家庭、社区与结构层次上相互作用的情境、心理社会、技术与习惯因素，设计并支持可持续的相关实践。它既不只是传递信息，也不只是建设设施。达罗安装水泵，期待行为随设备一同抵达；米娜发现，使用本身也是一套系统，由能力、机会、动机、信任、维护、社会意义，以及水泵明天仍会工作的重复经验共同建成。",
    "explanation": "WASH behaviour change supports sustained water, sanitation, and hygiene practices by addressing contextual, psychosocial, technological, and habitual determinants across several social levels.\n\nKnowledge and infrastructure matter, but so do capability, opportunity, motivation, trust, norms, maintenance, access, and equity. Effective interventions are locally investigated, co-designed, monitored, and revised.",
    "explanationZh": "水、环境卫生与个人卫生行为改变通过处理多个社会层次的情境、心理社会、技术与习惯因素，支持相关实践持续发生。\n\n知识与基础设施重要，能力、机会、动机、信任、规范、维护、可及与公平也同样重要。有效干预需要当地调查、共同设计、监测与修订。"
