    "explanation": "Normalization of deviance is the gradual acceptance of departures from safe or approved standards, reinforced when repeated exposure produces no immediate harm.\n\nProduction pressure, group culture, workarounds, and weak feedback can move the practical norm. Prevention requires credible reporting and stop authority, attention to weak signals, formal review of infeasible standards, and correction of system pressures.",
